## Gregory Vigil - Turn 4: Resolution
## Session Dialogue and Narration System (.session)
## Status: SKELETON - Content Pending

## =============================================================================
## TURN 4 OVERVIEW
## =============================================================================
## Time: 0:45-1:00 (final 15 minutes of session)
## Theme: Resolution
## Player Learns: Diagnosis submission, session conclusion, outcome feedback
##
## Key Story Beats:
## 1. Session Reflection - Brief recap of what was discussed
## 2. The Question - "So... what do you think is going on with me?"
## 3. Diagnosis Moment - Player submits their diagnosis
## 4. Gregory's Reaction - Varies based on accuracy and rapport
## 5. Looking Forward - Discussion of next steps, hope/concern
##
## Keywords to Introduce:
## - gregory.resolution.the_question
## - gregory.resolution.diagnosis_reaction
## - gregory.resolution.hope
## - gregory.resolution.next_steps
##
## This turn is primarily reactive to player's diagnosis
## =============================================================================

=== START ===

NARRATOR
*The session nears its end. Gregory shifts in his seat, expectant.*

@pause 0.5

@if rapport >= 60
    NARRATOR
    *There's a vulnerability in his expression now - anxiety, yes, but also perhaps relief at having been heard.*
@else
    NARRATOR
    *Gregory maintains his composed exterior, though his eyes betray uncertainty about what comes next.*
@endif

%His hands rest in his lap, fingers interlaced. Still. Waiting.%<symptom:controlled_stillness>

-> session_reflection

=== session_reflection ===

## Brief acknowledgment of the conversation that took place

PATIENT (thoughtful)
"We've talked about a lot today."

@pause 0.5

@if rapport >= 50
    PATIENT
    "More than I usually... I don't usually talk about this stuff."
    
    PATIENT (quiet)
    "With anyone."
@else
    PATIENT
    "I hope I gave you enough to work with."
    
    PATIENT (apologetic)
    "I know I tend to [ramble]<keyword:gregory.pattern.rambling>."
@endif

-> the_question

=== the_question ===

## KEY SCENE: Gregory asks for the diagnosis

NARRATOR
*Gregory takes a deep breath. The question he's been building toward.*

PATIENT (nervous)
"So..."

@pause 0.3

PATIENT (seeking)
"[What do you think is going on with me]<keyword:gregory.resolution.the_question>?"

%His eyes fix on you, a mixture of hope and fear in his gaze.%<symptom:expectant_gaze>

@pause 0.5

PATIENT (quickly)
"I mean, if you have an idea. If you've figured something out."

PATIENT (vulnerable)
"Is there... is there a [name]<keyword:gregory.resolution.wanting_name> for what I have?"

-> await_diagnosis

=== await_diagnosis ===

## SYSTEM: This is where the game prompts for diagnosis submission
## The following blocks trigger based on diagnosis result

NARRATOR
*The moment of assessment has arrived. Gregory waits.*

@prompt_diagnosis

## Continue to appropriate response block based on diagnosis

=== diagnosis_correct_high_rapport ===

## Correct diagnosis (GAD) with high rapport (60+)

NARRATOR
*You share your assessment: Generalized Anxiety Disorder.*

@pause 1

PATIENT (relieved)
"Generalized Anxiety Disorder..."

@pause 0.5

PATIENT
"I... I've wondered. If there was a [name]<keyword:gregory.resolution.relief_naming> for it."

%His shoulders drop slightly, tension releasing.%<symptom:tension_release>

PATIENT (vulnerable)
"Is it strange that I feel [relieved]<keyword:gregory.resolution.relief>? Like maybe I'm not 
just... broken or weak?"

@pause 0.5

PATIENT (grateful)
"Thank you. For listening. For not making me feel like 
I was [wasting your time]<keyword:gregory.resolution.validation>."

-> looking_forward_positive

=== diagnosis_correct_low_rapport ===

## Correct diagnosis (GAD) with low rapport (below 40)

NARRATOR
*You share your assessment: Generalized Anxiety Disorder.*

@pause 1

PATIENT (guarded)
"Generalized Anxiety Disorder. I see."

@pause 0.5

PATIENT
"I suppose that makes sense. Given what I told you."

%He nods slowly, processing. His expression remains carefully neutral.%<symptom:neutral_mask>

PATIENT (distant)
"So what happens now? Is there... is there something 
I'm [supposed to do]<keyword:gregory.resolution.uncertainty>?"

-> looking_forward_neutral

=== diagnosis_incorrect_high_rapport ===

## Wrong diagnosis with high rapport

NARRATOR
*You share your assessment. Gregory's expression shifts - confusion flickering across his face.*

@pause 1

PATIENT (confused)
"Oh. I... I'm not sure that quite [fits]<keyword:gregory.resolution.mismatch>."

@pause 0.5

PATIENT (apologetic)
"I'm sorry if I wasn't clear about things. Maybe I 
didn't [explain well enough]<keyword:gregory.resolution.self_blame>."

PATIENT (anxious)
"Should we... should we talk more? I feel like maybe 
I gave you the [wrong impression]<keyword:gregory.resolution.concern>."

-> looking_forward_uncertain

=== diagnosis_incorrect_low_rapport ===

## Wrong diagnosis with low rapport

NARRATOR
*You share your assessment. Gregory's jaw tightens almost imperceptibly.*

@pause 1

PATIENT (withdrawn)
"I don't think that's quite right."

@pause 0.5

PATIENT (flat)
"But you're the professional."

%His gaze drops to his hands. The distance between you feels larger now.%<symptom:withdrawal>

PATIENT (quiet)
"Maybe I should... think about what you've said."

-> looking_forward_disappointed

=== looking_forward_positive ===

## Positive conclusion - correct diagnosis, good rapport

PATIENT (hopeful)
"So... there's treatment? Things I can do?"

@pause 0.5

PATIENT
"I've spent so long thinking I just needed to try harder.
To be [better]<keyword:gregory.resolution.self_improvement>."

PATIENT (relieved)
"But if this is something... something real. With a name."

@pause 0.3

PATIENT (determined)
"Then maybe I can actually [work on it]<keyword:gregory.resolution.hope>."

NARRATOR
*For the first time today, something like genuine hope crosses Gregory's face.*

-> session_end

=== looking_forward_neutral ===

## Neutral conclusion - correct diagnosis, mediocre rapport

PATIENT (measured)
"I'll look into it. Treatment options, I mean."

PATIENT
"I appreciate your time today."

%He stands, smoothing his clothes - the careful, measured movements returning.%<symptom:controlled_behavior>

PATIENT (polite)
"Thank you for your assessment."

-> session_end

=== looking_forward_uncertain ===

## Uncertain conclusion - wrong diagnosis, high rapport

PATIENT (anxious)
"Maybe I should come back? Talk to someone else?"

@pause 0.5

PATIENT
"I don't mean... I'm not saying you did anything wrong."

PATIENT (spiraling)
"I just... I want to understand what's happening to me.
I [need]<keyword:gregory.resolution.desperate> to understand."

NARRATOR
*Gregory's earlier calm has fractured. The session ends with questions unanswered.*

-> session_end

=== looking_forward_disappointed ===

## Disappointed conclusion - wrong diagnosis, low rapport

PATIENT (flat)
"I should go."

@pause 0.5

NARRATOR
*Gregory rises stiffly. The careful composure has returned, but harder now. A wall rebuilt.*

PATIENT (distant)
"Thank you for your time."

%He doesn't meet your eyes as he gathers his things.%<symptom:avoidance>

-> session_end

=== session_end ===

## Final scene for all paths

NARRATOR
*The session concludes. Gregory moves toward the door.*

@if rapport >= 60 AND diagnosis_correct
    PATIENT (genuine)
    "I'll see you next time?"
    
    NARRATOR
    *A small smile - perhaps the first real one you've seen from him.*
@elseif diagnosis_correct
    PATIENT (polite)
    "Goodbye."
@else
    NARRATOR
    *Gregory leaves without another word. The door clicks shut behind him.*
@endif

-> END

=== END ===

NARRATOR
*The session with Gregory Vigil has concluded.*

